# Kia Sportage first generation five-door, 1995-2003.
#
# The original Sportage: the body-on-frame compact 4x4 based on Mazda Bongo
# mechanicals, with the separate chassis, the upright body and the tailgate-
# mounted spare. UK sales began in 1995 (Kia UK press office; RAC Drive).
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kia_Sportage
#
# Dimensions 4.245 x 1.730 x 1.650 m, wheelbase 2.650 m. The English
# Wikipedia infobox's 1.855 m width is 125 mm wider than three independent
# catalogues and wider than the 2010 car; 1.730 m is used and the discrepancy
# is recorded.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is a near-side
# view with the front face visible; the five-door body and external spare
# govern. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was found. Black, green, silver and red
# are plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 70/285, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 70: a tall,
# utilitarian body-on-frame cabin. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1995 intro, retires staggered 2014-2017.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/kia-sportage-1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: a thin dark bumper-corner tab is present in the
# three-quarter views but does not read at 128 px; the arch cladding is a heavy
# ring rather than a thin lip. The two-tone lower body is not modelled and the
# tailgate spare is a plain disc without carrier or cover. The greenhouse is
# shallower than the photograph's. At 128 px the boxy body, exposed spare and
# slotted grille read as a first-generation Sportage.


obj=citycar
name=KiaSportage1(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1995
intro_month=8
retire_year=2017
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=285

